15 . After the complainant rested his case vide order dated 25.01.2023, while the pre-summoning arguments were being addressed, Ld. Predecessor of this court thought it fit to direct ACP Hauz Khas to conduct a thorough investigation under section 202 Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (Cr.P.C) into the allegations of the complainant regarding the alleged incidents dated 19.07.2021 and 28-29/07/2021 and to report on the following aspects:
"(i) Location of the complainant, Ct.
'M' and respondent no.2 Ct.
Devender Yadav on 18.07.2021 to 19.07.2021 when the incident in question took place;
(ii) Location of house of the respondent no.2 and its distance from the spot of incident dated 19.07.2021;
(iii) Location of the complainant and Respondent no.2 during the intervening night of 28/29.07.2021 when the incident in question took place;
Manoj Kumar vs State Nct Of Delhi And Anr on 16 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93763691/
3 (iv) Hurling of casteist slurs at the complainant by the Respondent no.2 at the time of the two incidents in question as well as presence of public persons at the time of the said incidents;
(v) All other relevant details of the matter."
16.

Further, it is noted from the order dated 16.01.2024 that in regard to the inquiry report under section 202 Cr.P.C by ACP Harish Chander, at the instance of Ld. Counsel for the complainant, he proffered some clarifications as under:
"1. that the exact location of the alleged incident was not got identified by the complainant;
2. that the prosecutrix was though taken to place of incident but no site plan was prepared as she declined that she was dropped there;
3. that the location as per CDR could not be ascertained for 07am;
4. that no videography of inquiry was conducted as per under section 15A of SC/ST Act;
5. that no CDR of mobile no.838409XXXX of prosecutrix was placed on record;
6. that the alleged place of incident was not got physically verified from any independent witness."
